# React UI

- Functional components only. Match the file you are in (`export default` pages in `ecommerce-store/src/pages/`).
- Colocate feature state: existing `cartContext.jsx` / `orderContext.jsx` style. Do not add Redux/Zustand unless the spec requires it.
- Routing: `react-router-dom` `Routes` / `NavLink`. New screens need a route **and** nav/a11y name if they are user-facing.
- User-visible strings: keep tone of the current store/console; no hardcoded secrets in the client.
- States: implement empty, loading, and error when the spec names them. Do not leave a blank screen on failure.
- Accessibility: keep skip links, `aria-label` on icon-only controls, and real `<button>`/`<a>` (not clickable `div`s).
- Do not use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` or `bypassSecurityTrust*`. Encode dynamic text via React children.
- Styles: reuse existing CSS classes; do not drop in a new CSS framework for one screen.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD
<div onClick={go}>Cart</div>

// ✅ GOOD
<NavLink to="/cart" className="cart-link" aria-label={`Cart with ${count} items`}>
  Bag
</NavLink>
```
